# Project Architecture

Tool-Calling-Mini is a system for fine-tuning, serving, and interacting with a Qwen3 model specialized in tool calling. It consists of a training pipeline, an inference server, a tool execution engine, and two client interfaces.

## Component Map

```
Tool-Calling-Mini/
├── Model/                          Server: inference API + training pipeline + tools
│   ├── server.py                   FastAPI inference server (primary entry point)
│   ├── agent.py                    Multi-turn tool-call agent loop
│   ├── context.py                  Server-side token-aware context manager
│   ├── inference/                  Core inference, GGUF export, validation
│   ├── model_qwen4_finetuning/     Training pipeline, config.yaml, tool schemas
│   │   ├── config.yaml             SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for all configuration
│   │   ├── tool_calling_config.json  12 tool schemas (synced from homeassist-ref)
│   │   ├── data/                   Dataset preparation + training_data.jsonl
│   │   └── training/               QLoRA fine-tuning script
│   ├── tools/                      Tool implementations + validation + executor
│   ├── clients/                    External API clients used by tools
│   ├── tool_calling_sdk/           Shared SDK for conversation context management
│   └── homeassist-ref/             Git submodule — source of truth for tool definitions
├── Client-CLI/                     Terminal chat REPL with Rich UI
├── Client-Web/                     Web chat interface (React + FastAPI proxy)
│   ├── backend/                    FastAPI proxy with session management
│   └── frontend/                   React + TypeScript + Vite
├── Inference-Test-Suite/           Statistical accuracy validation against training data
├── scripts/                        Maintenance scripts (integration spec gen, git hooks)
├── INTEGRATION_API.md              Auto-generated external integration spec
└── README.md                       Project documentation
```

## Data Flow

```
User → Client (CLI or Web) → FastAPI server.py (:8000) → llama-server (:8080) → GPU inference
                                    ↓ tool_calls?
                              ToolExecutor → tool implementations → clients/ → External APIs
                                    ↓ tool results
                              Re-prompt model → final text response → Client
```

## Key Files to Know

| File | Why It Matters |
|------|---------------|
| `Model/model_qwen4_finetuning/config.yaml` | Central config for everything: models, LoRA, training, export, inference, agent |
| `Model/model_qwen4_finetuning/tool_calling_config.json` | Canonical tool schemas — used by training, inference, and INTEGRATION_API.md |
| `Model/server.py` | FastAPI server entry point — auth, endpoints, tool execution orchestration |
| `Model/agent.py` | Agent loop that drives multi-turn tool-call → result → re-prompt cycles |
| `Model/tools/models.py` | Pydantic validation models for all 12 tools with synonym normalization |
| `Model/tools/executor.py` | `ToolExecutor` — dispatches validated tool calls with timeout handling |
| `Model/inference/inference.py` | Prompt building, tool-call parsing, llama-server management |

## Authentication

All clients authenticate with the inference server using HMAC-SHA256 rotating API keys derived from `INFERENCE_REFRESH_TOKEN` (stored in `.env` files). Keys rotate every 5 minutes.

